<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian BNA bank starts venture fund.</title>
<headline>Tunisian BNA bank starts venture fund.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banque Nationale Agricole on Wednesday said it had launched a venture capital fund called SICAR INVEST.</p>
<p>It said the fund has a capital of 2.0 million dinars divided into 200,000 shares at 10 dinars each.</p>
<p>Venture capital funds called SICAR were first introduced in Tunisia in November 1995 to help reinforce the capital base of businesses for projects in priority sectors and regions. ($=1.07 dinar)</p>
<p>Tunis newsroom, 2161-787538</p>
</text>
